.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-thread-read - Read one message and, for a channel, its thread


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams thread read  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a message.  is a Teams message link, Team/Channel/MessageId,
Team/Channel/ or a chat message link. Channel threads are read with the
messages/{id} and messages/{id}/replies endpoints; chats have no threads, so a
chat message is shown on its own.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	fetch every page of replies

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for read

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=0
	maximum number of replies (0 means every page)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	only replies newer than this (a duration like 24h, or a timestamp)

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to (when the reference does not say)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	only replies older than this (a duration like 24h, or a timestamp)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams-thread(1)\fP
